Package: surface-camera
Version: 2.0
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-gst-plugins-base-1.0,
 gstreamer1.0-libcamera, gstreamer1.0-gtk4, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, libcamera-ipa, python3-numpy, python3-pil,
 gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0
Recommends: python3-zxing-cpp
Maintainer: chikara-linux <320610001+chikara-linux@users.noreply.github.com>
Description: Camera app for the Surface Go 2 IPU3 camera
 A touch friendly camera application that talks to libcamera directly
 through GStreamer's libcamerasrc, instead of going through PipeWire.
 .
 On this hardware the PipeWire camera node only advertises up to
 1280x720, while the front sensor can be driven at 2560x1920. Using
 libcamerasrc directly makes the full 5 megapixels available, which is
 what makes QR code scanning practical on a fixed focus front camera.
 .
 Photos are written to the Camera folder inside the user's Pictures
 directory. QR decoding uses python3-zxing-cpp, falling back to zbarimg if present.
